{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"100\t\n101\t`actor.id`/`actor.display` come from `git config user.email/name` at capture\n102\ttime. Default listings: own + unattributed conversations; `--all` shows every\n103\tauthor with labels. Transport is optional-but-default-on: Conversation\n104\tLedger's auto-installed pre-push hook and fetch refspec ride normal\n105\t`git push`/`git fetch`, gated by the ledger's secret scan and disableable per\n106\tuser (`{\"transport\": {\"hook\": false, \"fetchRefspec\": false}}`); `cledger sync`\n107\tremains available for an explicit push/fetch/merge. Turnbridge adds no\n108\tnetwork behavior of its own — it only reads whatever the ledger has already\n109\tabsorbed locally. Events captured before identity stamping existed are\n110\tunattributed; a forced transcript rescan after the upgrade can duplicate\n111\tthose turns under new event ids.\n112\t\n113\t## Risks\n114\t\n115\tNative formats change without notice (fabrication is version-pinned, bootstrap\n116\tis the recovery path); transcript content can include secrets (the ledger\n117\tredacts at capture and sync time, but matching is pattern/entropy-based and\n118\tcannot catch every secret — review before sharing still matters); full\n119\thistories can exceed the target's context (size is reported before launch);\n120\tcrashes mid-turn leave partial capture, which the ledger tolerates by design.\n121\t\n122\t## Roadmap\n123\t\n124\tToward an npm release (decided 2026-07-21; deepen the two existing targets\n125\tbefore broadening):\n126\t\n127\t- Publish `conversation-ledger` to npm (name is unclaimed), then swap the\n128\t  `file:` dependency for a semver range — `prepublishOnly` refuses to publish\n129\t  until this happens. Deliberately deferred while both packages are iterated\n130\t  on and dogfooded for a few days.\n131\t- Adapter-drift automation stage 2: the daily check\n132\t  (`.github/workflows/adapter-drift.yml`) currently opens a tracking issue on\n133\t  drift; the commented-out follow-on job hands the issue to a Claude Code\n134\t  action that revalidates the spec against the new CLI release and drafts the\n135\t  PR. Needs an `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` repo secret and comfort with CI pushing\n136\t  branches.\n137\t- Revalidation tooling exists and is the bar for widening version pins:\n138\t  `npm run smoke:interactive` (real-TUI render check, both targets) plus\n139\t  `scripts/probe-codex-content.mjs` (headless model-recall probe).\n140\t- Still-open verification gaps from the spec docs: large/long histories\n141\t  (size cliffs, Codex auto-compaction), timestamp-format tolerance,\n142\t  sessionId/filename mismatch, duplicate or dangling uuid handling.\n143\t- Encrypted-reasoning replay (2026-07-21 realization): Codex's `reasoning`\n144\t  items are ciphertext only OpenAI's servers can decrypt — the client just\n145\t  round-trips them, so recording them would let a fabricated Codex session\n146\t  restore hidden reasoning to the provider. Today they are lost twice over:\n147\t  the ledger drops them at capture (see Conversation Ledger's roadmap) and\n148\t  the fabricator omits them. This only bites fabricated codex-target\n149\t  sessions whose lineage began in Codex (different machine, deleted rollout,\n150\t  or a codex→claude→codex round trip) — same-CLI resume is native and keeps\n151\t  them. If the ledger starts preserving them, the fabricator should replay\n152\t  them only when source provider/CLI matches the target (never feed Codex\n153\t  blobs to Claude Code). Note the restore-policy space collapses to one\n154\t  switch: foreign/unreadable reasoning is already \"coerced\" in-band today by\n155\t  folding visible thinking into labeled text (safe, at the cost of possibly\n156\t  out-of-distribution context), and fabricating foreign reasoning as native\n157\t  reasoning *items* is impossible (ciphertext can't be forged) — so the only\n158\t  real option is whether provider-matched encrypted replay is on or off.\n159\t  Mixed-lineage sessions (codex→claude→codex) would then carry both: folded\n160\t  text for the Claude leg, replayed blobs for the Codex legs that match. Empirically verified via\n161\t  scripts/probe-encrypted-reasoning.mjs: same-account replay of a real blob\n162\t  in a fabricated session is accepted across sessions and CLI versions.\n163\t  Cross-account validity (teammate sharing): VERIFIED 2026-07-21 — a blob\n164\t  generated under one ChatGPT account replayed cleanly under a different\n165\t  paid ChatGPT account (identical token accounting to the owning-account\n166\t  run), so the ciphertext is not keyed per-account. Note the free tier\n167\t  cannot run Codex at all (entitlement 400s mask everything). Still open:\n168\t  blob TTL, and whether API-platform-org auth behaves the same as ChatGPT\n169\t  auth.\n170\t","tool_use_id":"toolu_01BBMZURxQRHDm5pigMMLGBH","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"a61d7e48f18594b62ae378267837151b1827b246","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:43ec7768-b4ea-485b-b6e2-ed60c3ad4a01","seq":50},"id":"ev1-3d13eff578feed18ecaf742c7e48175fe5ab3054a00b55537ede568221842a95","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-24T05:01:33.956Z","producer":{"session_id":"43ec7768-b4ea-485b-b6e2-ed60c3ad4a01","source":"claude-code","tool":"cledger","version":"0.10.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":"100\t\n101\t`actor.id`/`actor.display` come from `git config user.email/name` at capture\n102\ttime. Default listings: own + unattributed conversations; `--all` shows every\n103\tauthor with labels. Transport is optional-but-default-on: Conversation\n104\tLedger's auto-installed pre-push hook and f